1
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:17,537
The mafia boss with power across America,

2
00:00:17,587 --> 00:00:21,920
Don Castagnino, is the key piece
of evidence we need to convict him.

3
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:22,940
Key evidence?

4
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:25,900
Don Castagnino had

5
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:28,400
this boy's parents and siblings killed.

6
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,680
What?

7
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:33,380
This boy's father was an informant,

8
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:37,620
who tipped off the police
about Castagnino's drug deals.

9
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:41,120
Thanks to him, we were able to
arrest a lot of mafia members.

10
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,300
In retaliation, John's family?

11
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:48,920
Thanks to his mother's quick thinking,
before Castagnino's men burst in,

12
00:00:48,920 --> 00:00:51,340
John alone hid in the closet

13
00:00:51,340 --> 00:00:52,740
and escaped the danger.

14
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:06,720
Well, that's that.

15
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:18,560
You really went through hell, didn't you.

16
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:22,800
After that, Kasuta doll was
arrested in a different case,

17
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:27,520
but he's playing dumb, insisting he had
nothing to do with the murders of John's family.

18
00:01:27,520 --> 00:01:30,560
He doesn't know John witnessed it all,
of course.

19
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:33,520
So John's an important witness

20
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:39,260
So if John testifies in court that Kasuta
doll ordered the killing of his family,

21
00:01:39,260 --> 00:01:41,580
we can get that guy convicted, right?

22
00:01:42,540 --> 00:01:47,140
The trial is set for three days from now,
at the courthouse in LA.

23
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,680
Three days

24
00:01:54,100 --> 00:01:56,600
Alright, refueling's done,
you're good to go anytime.

25
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:57,620
Mister...

26
00:01:58,280 --> 00:01:59,540
Have a nice trip.

27
00:01:59,540 --> 00:02:02,380
Well, America's a great country, you know.

28
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:04,640
Bye!

29
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:44,860
I'll take you all the way there.

30
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:48,860
Well, this is a problem.

31
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:50,960
Will my English even get through?

32
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:52,640
That's part of it, but

33
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:55,360
John was so shocked by
his family being murdered

34
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:57,160
that he stopped being able to speak.

35
00:02:57,160 --> 00:02:59,820
When you say he can't speak,
does that mean he can't say anything at all?

36
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:00,600
Yes.

37
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:02,160
That's so sad.

38
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:03,280
Right.

39
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:09,880
How do you say "Sunday toy" in English?

40
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:10,820
Toy yo!

41
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:14,020
John, ken-der-my-es Japanese toy-der, okay?

42
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:15,600
Watch closely!

43
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:18,047
Ah, oof,

44
00:03:18,097 --> 00:03:20,326
Ori eh,

45
00:03:20,376 --> 00:03:22,394
Yo, whoa, haha,

46
00:03:22,444 --> 00:03:24,700
See, pretty good, right?

47
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:27,520
Hey, you try it too woah -

48
00:03:27,520 --> 00:03:31,060
John, what are you doing!

49
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:34,280
Ryo-san is on your side, put away the knife!

50
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:40,880
Honestly, American brats are so unlovable.

51
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,560
Ryo-san, please forgive him.

52
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,880
I went through the same
thing when I first met him.

53
00:03:47,300 --> 00:03:50,180
He thinks all adults are his enemies.

54
00:03:51,340 --> 00:03:52,700
Well, I suppose that's understandable.

55
00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:58,980
But why are we driving all the way to LA?

56
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:01,620
Flying would be faster and safer, right?

57
00:04:01,620 --> 00:04:03,800
Kennedy Airport, of course,

58
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:08,920
the factories, the helipads,
and every railway station,

59
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:13,060
We've received intel that Don Castanine's
henchmen are swarming everywhere.

60
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:14,144
I see.

61
00:04:14,194 --> 00:04:18,360
Naturally, to silence John,
the key to proving the boss guilty,

62
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:20,620
so they've set up an ambush

63
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:23,240
Yes. It's three days to LA, but

64
00:04:23,320 --> 00:04:24,728
that's why we're in disguise like this,

65
00:04:24,778 --> 00:04:28,020
It's better to pose as a
carefree family on vacation,

66
00:04:28,040 --> 00:04:29,820
so they won't notice us, they said.

67
00:04:30,220 --> 00:04:30,540
Yeah.

68
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,280
What's wrong?

69
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,659
I thought they wouldn't notice,

70
00:04:33,709 --> 00:04:36,300
but it looks like that didn't work.
Look behind you.

71
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:40,760
Oh no, a whole bunch of
trouble is coming at us!

72
00:04:43,640 --> 00:04:44,360
Don't freeze up!

73
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:46,880
Mm-hmm.

74
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:49,850
Whoa,

75
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:52,580
seriously?

76
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:04,560
Can't back up either. What do we do?

77
00:05:09,520 --> 00:05:13,280
Damn it,
at this rate we'll be completely crushed!

78
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,220
Alright!

79
00:05:14,220 --> 00:05:14,920
Ryo-san!

80
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:16,580
Nice!

81
00:05:23,780 --> 00:05:24,820
You bastard!

82
00:05:29,380 --> 00:05:30,420
Ryo-san!

83
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:35,326
Don't get cocky!

84
00:05:35,376 --> 00:05:39,100
Officer Ryo won't be taken
down by something like this!

85
00:05:42,100 --> 00:05:43,560
Aaaaah!

86
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:44,360
Aaaaah!

87
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:44,800
Aaaaah!

88
00:05:44,800 --> 00:05:45,760
Aaaaah!

89
00:05:45,760 --> 00:05:46,940
Aaaaah!

90
00:05:46,940 --> 00:05:48,080
John! Where's Ryo-san?

91
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:53,760
N-...

92
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:55,600
What? What's wrong?

93
00:06:04,060 --> 00:06:05,020
I can't see ahead!

94
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:05,700
Whoa!

95
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:06,640
Hyaaah!

96
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,600
Sunday, are you okay?

97
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:10,740
Ryo-san, you're safe!

98
00:06:10,820 --> 00:06:12,360
This car was mine, I was driving it!

99
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:15,040
I'll clear the way, so floor it!

100
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:15,940
Got it!

101
00:06:16,700 --> 00:06:17,100
Right!

102
00:06:17,360 --> 00:06:18,000
Here we go!

103
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:19,360
Sunday!

104
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:20,260
Now!

105
00:06:20,500 --> 00:06:20,980
Okay!

106
00:06:23,340 --> 00:06:24,340
Alright! Let's go!

107
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:25,280
Sunday!

108
00:06:29,400 --> 00:06:31,400
Right! Next is the one behind us!

109
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:45,680
Ryo-san

110
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:49,520
Ryo-san

111
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:51,660
Yeah, I'm here.

112
00:06:52,200 --> 00:06:54,380
Ryo-san

113
00:06:54,380 --> 00:06:58,360
I'm fine, but I lost a sandal.

114
00:06:59,680 --> 00:07:00,560
Thank goodness.

115
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:04,300
This divine wind really

116
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:12,640
It's hopeless.
Not just the body, the engine's gone too.

117
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:13,800
It can't be helped.

118
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:17,580
Let's leave this car
here and rent another one.

119
00:07:17,940 --> 00:07:20,360
Where are we supposed to rent a car?

120
00:07:20,360 --> 00:07:23,120
We can't even see a single house,
let alone a town.

121
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:28,320
I'll hitchhike to the
nearest town and rent one.

122
00:07:28,660 --> 00:07:29,660
Hitchhike?

123
00:07:30,740 --> 00:07:32,020
Here it comes.

124
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:36,300
You two stay hidden behind the car, okay?

125
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:37,880
Why?

126
00:07:38,680 --> 00:07:41,100
Cars won't stop for a woman traveling with kids,
will they?

127
00:07:41,460 --> 00:07:41,780
I see.

128
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:56,720
What power!

129
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,260
He's gone.

130
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:13,600
We've got time to kill
until Sunday gets back.

131
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:19,620
Corn stalks

132
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:22,360
Bird netting...

133
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:25,060
I've got a good idea!

134
00:08:26,720 --> 00:08:27,200
Lend me that.

135
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:28,940
A knife, a knife!

136
00:08:32,500 --> 00:08:33,340
Thanks.

137
00:08:36,600 --> 00:08:38,120
How's that? Funny

138
00:08:38,540 --> 00:08:40,800
John, go get that net over there.

139
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:42,860
The net, the net!

140
00:08:42,860 --> 00:08:45,560
There's bird netting in
that field over there, right?

141
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:48,600
Here, take this and go dampen it a little.

142
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:52,260
Like this, like this.

143
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:53,740
There, it's done!

144
00:09:07,580 --> 00:09:08,600
How about it, John?

145
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,980
That Japanese kite octopus
is pretty good, right?

146
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:14,460
So you like it

147
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:19,200
Finally, here comes Sunday.

148
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:24,620
Ryo-san, I bought sandals too.

149
00:09:25,300 --> 00:09:27,080
Thanks.

150
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,440
That was fun.

151
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:33,780
It's fine, that's a present for you.

152
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:38,000
You two got pretty close while I was gone

153
00:09:38,460 --> 00:09:39,060
Well, yeah.

154
00:09:39,960 --> 00:09:40,920
Anyway, Sunday.

155
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:44,920
From here on, I think we should
avoid stopping anywhere if we can.

156
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:47,260
The fact that we're using this road

157
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:50,060
seems to have already been
figured out by them, so.

158
00:09:50,060 --> 00:09:50,860
Right.

159
00:09:51,240 --> 00:09:54,400
But driving straight through
for three days is impossible.

160
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:57,180
If we take turns with me and grab naps,

161
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,520
we can make it nonstop.

162
00:09:58,520 --> 00:09:59,500
Okay.

163
00:10:30,760 --> 00:10:31,340
That's right!

164
00:10:32,460 --> 00:10:34,820
Yeah! Jan! You try it too!

165
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,340
Whoa! You're too soft, Jan!

166
00:10:39,540 --> 00:10:40,420
Good! Good!

167
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:48,052
What's up,

168
00:10:48,102 --> 00:10:51,430
you two?

169
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:57,520
You haven't eaten at all.

170
00:10:57,980 --> 00:11:00,800
I'm so tired I don't have an appetite.

171
00:11:00,800 --> 00:11:04,180
Come to think of it, we've been
driving non-stop for over two days.

172
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:08,440
Then let's find a place to stay
tonight and get some proper rest.

173
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:10,700
They probably haven't realized that
we're traveling in a rental car,

174
00:11:10,700 --> 00:11:13,060
so they probably haven't noticed.

175
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:15,860
Yeah, and we've already entered California,

176
00:11:16,200 --> 00:11:20,840
so if we leave first thing in the morning,
we'll easily make it before the trial starts.

177
00:11:21,840 --> 00:11:23,580
Alright, then once I finish eating,

178
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:25,060
let's go look for a place to sleep.

179
00:11:25,620 --> 00:11:27,200
Aren't you going to eat that chili beans?

180
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,340
Mind if I have it?

181
00:11:29,680 --> 00:11:30,400
Hehe.

182
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:34,420
Come on, let's go.

183
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,500
Listen, John.

184
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:59,520
You're sleeping right here, like this.

185
00:12:00,300 --> 00:12:01,980
And Sunday's in the middle.

186
00:12:01,980 --> 00:12:02,760
Center.

187
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:08,840
You don't need to know why.

188
00:12:08,840 --> 00:12:10,960
Anyway,
we're sleeping in that order, got it?

189
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,280
As long as John falls asleep,

190
00:12:15,280 --> 00:12:19,060
I can do all sorts of things with Sunday.

191
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:23,960
What's with that look?

192
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:26,180
Enough, you little brat,
go to sleep already.

193
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:29,400
The LA police contacted me.

194
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:33,000
They said they'll send an
escort before we leave tomorrow.

195
00:12:34,460 --> 00:12:37,060
Well then, I think I'll take a shower.

196
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:38,240
Wait.

197
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:41,740
Before that, could you ask
Colonel Bakuryu for backup too?

198
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:44,060
If John testifies,

199
00:12:44,060 --> 00:12:46,600
Don Castanine is sure to be convicted,
you know.

200
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:48,740
his underlings will be desperate,

201
00:12:48,740 --> 00:12:51,520
I think they'll come to
stop us from getting into LA.

202
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,340
I see.

203
00:12:52,340 --> 00:12:53,380
Got it.

204
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:56,060
Then, Sunday, take a shower and wait for us.

205
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:57,400
Wait for us.

206
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:59,480
No, no, never mind.

207
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:01,160
I'll call right away.

208
00:13:08,220 --> 00:13:11,000
Who's calling at this hour?

209
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:13,420
It's me, Kankichi Ryotsu!

210
00:13:13,420 --> 00:13:14,800
It's you.

211
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:16,580
What's wrong?

212
00:13:20,480 --> 00:13:21,640
Did something happen?

213
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:30,480
Achoo!

214
00:13:34,420 --> 00:13:36,520
What are you guys doing?

215
00:13:36,560 --> 00:13:37,860
Ryo-san

216
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:39,440
Too bad.

217
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:40,500
John

218
00:13:41,060 --> 00:13:48,840
Shit.

219
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:59,220
Damn it.

220
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,200
You bastard, you did this.

221
00:14:01,200 --> 00:14:01,900
Achoo!

222
00:14:04,160 --> 00:14:04,720
John

223
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,300
Sunday

224
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:06,780
That's right.

225
00:14:09,880 --> 00:14:10,400
Hello?

226
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:11,160
Ryotsu?

227
00:14:11,460 --> 00:14:12,660
What was that noise just now?

228
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:13,960
Talk later.

229
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:15,380
Just come quickly.

230
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:23,960
Shit.

231
00:14:24,260 --> 00:14:24,920
It's a beast!

232
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:28,480
This goddamn bastard
must've pulled some strings.

233
00:14:37,180 --> 00:14:38,240
Where the hell are you going?

234
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:41,140
There's an old warehouse up
ahead that nobody uses anymore.

235
00:14:49,980 --> 00:14:53,260
Yeah, where the hell
did that red trailer go?

236
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:56,600
The police are running
checkpoints on every road.

237
00:14:57,040 --> 00:14:59,040
They can't possibly get out of this city.

238
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:02,020
Sanze, John, please stay safe.

239
00:15:11,540 --> 00:15:12,980
Are you just going to sit quietly here?

240
00:15:27,500 --> 00:15:30,000
Batracky's brother said to kill him, but

241
00:15:30,380 --> 00:15:31,440
we don't have to do that?

242
00:15:31,900 --> 00:15:33,720
We just need to miss the trial.

243
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:35,940
Leave it to your brother, it's fine.

244
00:15:41,840 --> 00:15:43,320
You've got the Jaws of Life, right?

245
00:15:48,180 --> 00:15:49,520
Yeah, let me borrow it for a sec.

246
00:16:01,920 --> 00:16:03,920
Got it! Come on, hurry!

247
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:05,800
Please.

248
00:16:15,160 --> 00:16:16,440
It won't open any wider?

249
00:16:16,960 --> 00:16:18,860
Then there's no way out from there.

250
00:16:25,280 --> 00:16:26,980
What do you plan to do with a kite?

251
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:29,360
With that?

252
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:33,140
I see, good idea, John.

253
00:16:34,860 --> 00:16:37,360
So what are the police doing?

254
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:40,100
At this rate,
we won't make it to today's trial.

255
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:43,600
What is that?

256
00:16:45,820 --> 00:16:46,600
It's John!

257
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:48,900
It's the kite I made for John.

258
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:56,260
Found it at last!

259
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,460
Land somewhere they won't notice us.

260
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:00,480
Got it.

261
00:17:03,180 --> 00:17:06,000
Less than an hour from now, and they
don't even know they're about to be killed.

262
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:07,500
Look at him, sleeping like a log.

263
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:13,740
It's okay.

264
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:15,220
We found that octopus -

265
00:17:15,620 --> 00:17:17,660
Ryo-san will surely come to save us.

266
00:17:18,020 --> 00:17:18,940
He's already here.

267
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:20,800
Ryo-san?

268
00:17:22,640 --> 00:17:24,780
Sunday, how many enemies are there?

269
00:17:24,780 --> 00:17:25,540
Two.

270
00:17:28,020 --> 00:17:29,820
Right, we don't have much
time before the trial.

271
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:32,340
It'll get a little rough,
but I'll save you right away.

272
00:17:32,340 --> 00:17:34,600
Move over to that corner and stay down.

273
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:35,820
Got it.

274
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:43,520
Please!

275
00:17:43,520 --> 00:17:44,380
Okay!

276
00:17:48,400 --> 00:17:49,200
What?

277
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,320
Run!

278
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:51,740
Wait!

279
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:53,020
Jan, this way!

280
00:17:53,020 --> 00:17:54,680
Run, run!

281
00:17:56,020 --> 00:17:56,820
Jaan!

282
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:01,220
Aaaaaah!

283
00:18:01,850 --> 00:18:02,500
Jan!

284
00:18:02,930 --> 00:18:03,620
Don't move!

285
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:06,340
Get 'em!

286
00:18:06,960 --> 00:18:07,900
Don't shoot!

287
00:18:16,340 --> 00:18:16,820
Jaan!

288
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:19,400
Jaan!

289
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,100
Jaan!

290
00:18:20,550 --> 00:18:21,180
Jaan!

291
00:18:21,460 --> 00:18:21,800
Jaan!

292
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:25,190
Aaagh!

293
00:18:32,450 --> 00:18:48,650
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

294
00:18:48,650 --> 00:18:51,310
You actually killed John, didn't you!

295
00:18:52,650 --> 00:18:54,090
Stop it, Ryotsu!

296
00:18:54,090 --> 00:18:55,450
Let go, Colonel!

297
00:18:55,450 --> 00:18:58,110
I understand how you feel,
but don't go any further!

298
00:18:58,110 --> 00:18:59,070
Damn it!

299
00:18:59,510 --> 00:19:00,330
Ryo-san!

300
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:03,610
John's alive!

301
00:19:05,010 --> 00:19:05,450
What?

302
00:19:05,950 --> 00:19:06,750
John!

303
00:19:06,750 --> 00:19:07,670
John!

304
00:19:08,930 --> 00:19:10,790
How did you...

305
00:19:14,830 --> 00:19:15,670
Beigoma!

306
00:19:16,190 --> 00:19:20,070
The beigoma Ryo-san gave him protected John!

307
00:19:20,930 --> 00:19:21,850
Ryo-san...

308
00:19:22,410 --> 00:19:23,350
What is it, John?

309
00:19:23,940 --> 00:19:24,590
John!

310
00:19:24,590 --> 00:19:26,450
Ryo-san...

311
00:19:26,450 --> 00:19:29,790
Did you learn how to talk?

312
00:19:30,450 --> 00:19:32,250
Thank you, Ryo-san.

313
00:19:32,250 --> 00:19:35,310
Thank goodness, thank goodness.

314
00:19:37,430 --> 00:19:38,890
Thank goodness, thank goodness.

315
00:19:53,330 --> 00:19:54,050
Your Honor.

316
00:19:54,710 --> 00:19:57,910
We cannot wait any longer for
the prosecution's witnesses.

317
00:19:59,610 --> 00:20:02,370
If there are no witnesses,
proceed to the next item.

318
00:20:03,370 --> 00:20:04,730
We've got a witness right here!

319
00:20:05,950 --> 00:20:06,310
What?

320
00:20:11,070 --> 00:20:12,130
W-what?

321
00:20:13,650 --> 00:20:16,110
Your Honor, I'm late, but I'm the witness.

322
00:20:16,110 --> 00:20:18,450
Please allow me to question the witness.

323
00:20:24,530 --> 00:20:31,270
Who ordered the killing of John's family,
the Wilsons?

324
00:20:39,450 --> 00:20:40,070
Do it.

325
00:20:41,770 --> 00:20:42,830
This is the man.

326
00:20:44,230 --> 00:20:46,730
Liar! What this brat is saying is nonsense!

327
00:20:46,730 --> 00:20:50,010
Something like this... I have an alibi.

328
00:20:50,790 --> 00:20:51,150
Hey!

329
00:20:54,610 --> 00:20:57,030
With this, that Castanya guy is finished

330
00:20:57,030 --> 00:20:59,970
Yes, life imprisonment is certain.

331
00:21:05,530 --> 00:21:06,950
Well then, everyone.

332
00:21:06,950 --> 00:21:09,310
Mar-chan, you're hurt too,
yet you're seeing us off. Sorry.

333
00:21:09,310 --> 00:21:10,990
It's just a scratch.

334
00:21:10,990 --> 00:21:13,110
John, let's meet again.

335
00:21:13,110 --> 00:21:13,550
Yeah.

336
00:21:15,710 --> 00:21:18,130
Ryo-san, thank you so much.

337
00:21:18,590 --> 00:21:20,110
I don't know how to thank you enough.

338
00:21:20,110 --> 00:21:22,290
Well then, Sunday,
a kiss will do for you too.

339
00:21:23,230 --> 00:21:24,170
Okay.

340
00:21:24,890 --> 00:21:25,910
No...

341
00:21:34,590 --> 00:21:36,170
Alright, my turn next.

342
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:39,810
Mar-chan, you're fine,
but watch out, you'll hurt your wound!

343
00:21:39,810 --> 00:21:40,550
I see.

344
00:21:41,050 --> 00:21:41,990
That's a shame.

345
00:21:45,050 --> 00:21:45,930
Well, see you.

346
00:21:45,930 --> 00:21:47,850
Take care, Ryo-chan.

347
00:21:47,850 --> 00:21:49,870
I'm definitely coming to Japan, you know.

348
00:21:49,870 --> 00:21:51,250
Goodbye, Ryo-san.

349
00:21:52,350 --> 00:21:54,010
Welcome back, senpai.

350
00:21:54,010 --> 00:21:55,310
Nakagawa.

351
00:21:55,310 --> 00:21:56,550
You look well.

352
00:21:56,550 --> 00:21:56,750
Yeah, I suppose so.

353
00:21:56,750 --> 00:21:57,950
Of course I am.

354
00:21:57,950 --> 00:22:00,630
I didn't do a lick of work for two weeks,
after all.

355
00:22:01,150 --> 00:22:04,050
Did you check your souvenirs at the airport?

356
00:22:04,050 --> 00:22:05,250
No, not really.

357
00:22:06,290 --> 00:22:08,710
I bought G.I. Joe and an
American Pango Godzilla,

358
00:22:08,710 --> 00:22:10,570
but I ended up giving them to John.

359
00:22:11,050 --> 00:22:14,050
Didn't you bring anything back for
the Chief or the Director either?

360
00:22:14,050 --> 00:22:15,070
Was that a mistake?

361
00:22:15,490 --> 00:22:18,270
After Reiko went to all the trouble
of warning you about everything, too.

362
00:22:18,270 --> 00:22:19,190
I see.

363
00:22:20,990 --> 00:22:23,390
Alright, Nakagawa, lend me some money.

364
00:22:24,550 --> 00:22:26,130
Welcome back, Ryo-chan.

365
00:22:26,570 --> 00:22:28,390
Chief, I'm back.

366
00:22:28,390 --> 00:22:32,170
Did anything give you
trouble while I was away?

367
00:22:32,690 --> 00:22:35,870
Thanks to you, everything went smoothly.

368
00:22:35,870 --> 00:22:39,250
Go again sometime, to Alaska,
for about fifty years.

369
00:22:40,070 --> 00:22:41,170
That's a harsh joke.

370
00:22:41,630 --> 00:22:43,770
You bought souvenirs for the Chief and the others,
didn't you?

371
00:22:43,770 --> 00:22:46,650
Of course I did, in America!

372
00:22:46,650 --> 00:22:50,590
Then I'll go to the station
first and hand out the souvenirs.

373
00:22:51,190 --> 00:22:52,130
Hold on a second.

374
00:22:52,130 --> 00:22:52,310
Gulp!

375
00:22:52,810 --> 00:22:54,870
Let me see what you bought.

376
00:22:56,550 --> 00:22:57,850
So suspicious!

377
00:22:57,850 --> 00:23:00,370
The list said liquor for the Chief, so

378
00:23:00,370 --> 00:23:01,450
It's liquor, to be exact.

379
00:23:02,730 --> 00:23:04,790
That's a pretty big whisky.

380
00:23:06,030 --> 00:23:06,430
Hey!

381
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:10,890
It says "Otokozakari" on it!

382
00:23:10,890 --> 00:23:12,990
Made with California rice.

383
00:23:12,990 --> 00:23:14,290
It's made purely in America.

384
00:23:14,290 --> 00:23:17,170
You bought sake in America?
What were you thinking?

385
00:23:17,170 --> 00:23:18,710
Show me the other souvenirs too.

386
00:23:18,710 --> 00:23:19,450
Ehh...

387
00:23:19,450 --> 00:23:21,470
For the deputy chief, a crazy doll.

388
00:23:21,470 --> 00:23:23,270
For the community section chief, a camera.

389
00:23:23,270 --> 00:23:26,490
For the inspector section chief,
I bought a Kiyomizu-yaki tea bowl.

390
00:23:27,610 --> 00:23:30,110
And last but not least, the Chief.

391
00:23:30,110 --> 00:23:31,330
Ta-da!

392
00:23:31,330 --> 00:23:33,970
Hakata obi and a zōri set, to be exact.

393
00:23:34,550 --> 00:23:37,630
Did you really go to America?

394
00:23:37,630 --> 00:23:40,150
Weren't you just hiding out in Tokyo?

395
00:23:40,710 --> 00:23:43,490
These are all things I bought in America.

396
00:23:43,490 --> 00:23:47,090
They're so-called reverse imports,
really rare items.

397
00:23:47,690 --> 00:23:49,790
Well then,
I'll ask you about the broadcast sheet:

398
00:23:49,790 --> 00:23:53,770
why does it say
"Shin-Tokyo International Airport"?

399
00:23:53,770 --> 00:23:55,510
No, that's not right.

400
00:23:55,510 --> 00:23:58,190
That's not Tokyo, it's Tonkin.

401
00:23:58,190 --> 00:24:02,390
We made a stopover in Tonkin, next to Beijing,
on the way back, so that's where it -

402
00:24:02,910 --> 00:24:05,110
Do you really think you
can fool me with that?

403
00:24:05,570 --> 00:24:06,350
Ryo-chan.

404
00:24:08,010 --> 00:24:10,350
You haven't filled in the
travel log at all, either.

405
00:24:11,230 --> 00:24:13,970
Details like that are
just not my strong suit.

406
00:24:13,970 --> 00:24:17,770
What happened to the letter of introduction
Chief Tonda wrote to the chief over there?

407
00:24:17,770 --> 00:24:21,410
That one?
I've got it right here, just as I said.

408
00:24:22,370 --> 00:24:25,530
You idiot!
It's pointless if you don't hand it over!

409
00:24:25,890 --> 00:24:27,870
Hey, stop right there, Ryotsu!

410
00:24:29,150 --> 00:24:31,450
Overseas training, that's -

411
00:24:31,500 --> 00:24:33,850
I'm sick of all you idiots!

